VISUAL: The speaker introduces the topic of websites becoming irrelevant in the age of AI search.
AUDIO: 'The CEO of Google, Sundarbachai, said in a recent&nbsp; interview that 2027 is the year of the agents.&nbsp;&nbsp; At the same time, 58% of Google searches end&nbsp; with no clicks. That means over half the people&nbsp;&nbsp; that are going to Google and searching for things&nbsp; never end up on a website. They\'re getting their&nbsp;&nbsp; answers from AI. In this video, I\'ll show you why&nbsp; websites will matter dramatically less over the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'next 3 years, what\'s replacing them, and what home&nbsp; service businesses should be building right now to&nbsp;&nbsp; stay ahead. I\'ve been doing digital marketing for&nbsp; home service businesses for eight years and I can&nbsp;&nbsp; tell you that this is the biggest shift from an&nbsp; agency perspective, from a business perspective.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
